<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Washington returns two weeks after the sick visit for community-acquired pneumonia. At the 48-hour phone check his fever had broken; he finished five days of amoxicillin without rash or diarrhea. He has had no fever for eleven days. A mild dry cough remains in the mornings, and he tires more easily than before, but he has no breathlessness walking or on the stairs and no chest pain. He took a week off work and is back to half days. His appetite fell during the illness and his weight is 92.9 kg, down 1.3 kg from six weeks ago; he has gone back to the supplement twice a day. The implant sites are comfortable and the soft-lined lower denture fits well. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pneumonia</td><td>Afebrile for eleven days; mild morning cough; tiring easily</td></tr><tr><td>Amoxicillin</td><td>Five-day course completed; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>92.9 kg, down 1.3 kg during the illness</td></tr><tr><td>Implants</td><td>Comfortable; attachments planned in four weeks</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

